I used to be terrified by mumaks until my fairly unprepared character
was stuck at a T-junction next to one, with another monster on each of
the other branches (not my own fault, some rotten swine with a c?CM).
As a last resort, I decided to break a wand of light for the chance of
blinding everything nearby.  The blast killed the (freshly-generated)
mumak, and the character reached the stairs safely.

This led me to the conclusion that while mumaks can dish out an
uncomfortable amount of damage, they don't take much.

